From 150d4043e7c0841ad32f62eff3845cc0bf9231c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:34:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: use the corrected end-to-end prompt in the chain
 example

The example carried the exact trigger the section's own warning says makes
a chain case false-pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
---
 docs/skill-authoring.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/skill-authoring.md b/docs/skill-authoring.md
index dfb66b93eb..d9208e9303 100644
--- a/docs/skill-authoring.md
+++ b/docs/skill-authoring.md
@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@ A chained case names the ordered skills one run should load:
 
 ```json
 {
-  "prompt": "Write an integration test that exercises tool listing against a real server.",
+  "prompt": "Write an integration test that exercises tool listing end to end.",
   "chain": ["testing", "test-servers"]
 }
 ```
